to {0}^{-}}g(x)=0\\ne -2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x)=-2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-38547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d761c983c50a4f38a80dc31b40a48f91f79070868f6f3a212d0b95189cadba11"} {"question" "q-38547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-38547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-38547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/assets/89dca4b059ccbd1fe93d000acabcbd33b5fc10389de48ef3cbae65cb4455f29e.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne 3=f(1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)=1\\ne 3=f(1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d761c983c50a4f38a80dc31b40a48f91f79070868f6f3a212d0b95189cadba11"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-73106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the statements are true"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-5$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)=3,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}(f(x)-2f(-5))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-5,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)=f(-5)=3.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}(f(x)-2f(-5)) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-5)^{+}}f(x)-2f(-5) \\\\  & =3-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d761c983c50a4f38a80dc31b40a48f91f79070868f6f3a212d0b95189cadba11"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104283" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-6,$ then what is \n${lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(2f(x)-xf(-1))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=f(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(2f(x)-xf(-1)) & =2{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)-f(-1){lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}x \\\\  & =2(-6)-(-6)(-1) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d761c983c50a4f38a80dc31b40a48f91f79070868f6f3a212d0b95189cadba11"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-18"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"} {"question" "q-104286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008055/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b4ed42ea65d91fd2df0b85f6618fca6bd2696b2444645c57ea2bc323876eb49"}] "usage" {"q-38547" []} "basis" 1131 "retractions" [[17592186069234 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer